  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The abstract does not present empirical data, quantitative metrics, or a specific case study evaluation of a built project.",
      "what": "This paper explores the integration of Indigenous knowledge systems with landscape architecture to design therapeutic outdoor environments. It examines how traditional ecological practices and cultural connections to land can be systematically incorporated into modern spatial design to support community health and wellbeing.",
      "why": "It establishes a conceptual framework for landscape designers to move beyond purely Western, clinical models of therapeutic space, offering a structured approach to co-designing environments that address cultural displacement and support healing through indigenous land relations."
    }
